WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.840 --> 00:00:06.280
Let's pray together over day 23.

2
00:00:06.820 --> 00:00:08.020
Holiness is a completing

3
00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:09.500
of the project.

4
00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:15.630
This prayer is from St. Augustine of Hippo in 350.

5
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:17.850
He lived from 354 to 430.

6
00:00:19.460 --> 00:00:23.360
"Lord Jesus, let me know myself and know thee, and desire

7
00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:25.140
nothing save only thee.

8
00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:30.090
Let me hate myself and love thee. Let me do everything for the sake of

9
00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:30.340
thee.

10
00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:33.280
Let me humble myself and exalt thee.

11
00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:35.960
Let me think of nothing except thee.

12
00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:40.140
Let me die to myself and live in thee.

13
00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:42.780
Let me accept whatever happens as from thee.

14
00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:47.320
Let me banish self and follow thee, and ever desire

15
00:00:47.740 --> 00:00:48.460
to follow thee.

16
00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:53.320
Let me fly from myself and take refuge in thee, that I may

17
00:00:53.380 --> 00:00:55.180
deserve to be defended by thee.

18
00:00:56.240 --> 00:00:59.940
Let me fear for myself, let me fear thee, and let me be

19
00:00:59.980 --> 00:01:02.020
among those who are chosen by thee.

20
00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:06.000
Let me distrust myself and put my trust in thee.

21
00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:09.280
Let me be willing to obey for the sake of thee.

22
00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:12.560
Let me cling to nothing save only to thee,

23
00:01:14.050 --> 00:01:15.900
and let me be poor because of thee.

24
00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:20.280
Look upon me that I may love thee. Call me that I may see

25
00:01:20.360 --> 00:01:22.780
thee and forever enjoy thee."

26
00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:28.330
Father, we are thankful for your beautiful

27
00:01:28.360 --> 00:01:32.200
holiness. It is more desirable and satisfying than

28
00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:36.140
anything else in all the world. We thank you for giving it

29
00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:39.840
to us. We thank you for providing holiness for us.

30
00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:43.200
We rejoice in the promises, Lord, the promises of God,

31
00:01:44.020 --> 00:01:46.380
that everything that you are

32
00:01:47.220 --> 00:01:51.130
and you will be for us is contained in this holiness

33
00:01:51.220 --> 00:01:54.140
that you have given to us. And Lord, we want to experience

34
00:01:54.840 --> 00:01:57.970
everything there is to know about those promises.

35
00:01:58.020 --> 00:02:01.850
We want all of it, Lord. So we turn away from

36
00:02:01.940 --> 00:02:03.600
all filthiness of flesh,

37
00:02:04.420 --> 00:02:08.320
all filthiness of spirit. We turn away from lust

38
00:02:08.380 --> 00:02:11.021
and pride and arrogance and self-will.

39
00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:15.580
We turn away from self-pity, and we turn away from all

40
00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:19.520
that is corrupted by me, the great I at the center of our

41
00:02:19.540 --> 00:02:19.750
soul.

42
00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:24.440
And we pray, O God, that you would help us to have the

43
00:02:24.460 --> 00:02:27.250
strength to repudiate it and that you would cleanse us now.

44
00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:31.180
Go deep and let the power of the Holy

45
00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:34.900
Spirit cleanse us from all filthiness of flesh and spirit, and

46
00:02:35.020 --> 00:02:38.920
perfect, complete, bring to fullness the holiness that you've begun

47
00:02:39.020 --> 00:02:39.400
for us.

48
00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:43.120
Let's continue praying now and seeking the Lord together.
